WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.065 --> 00:00:01.236
- Good morning, believe nation.

00:00:01.236 --> 00:00:05.189
Today's message is make
something people want.

00:00:05.189 --> 00:00:06.745
Over to you, Sam Altman.

00:00:06.745 --> 00:00:08.848
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.848 --> 00:00:11.501
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:14.327
♫ Espresso get me going

00:00:14.327 --> 00:00:18.244
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.244 --> 00:00:19.407
- Startups, to be successful,

00:00:19.407 --> 00:00:21.698
have to build something that people want.

00:00:21.698 --> 00:00:24.971
If you get that right, you
can get everything else wrong.

00:00:24.971 --> 00:00:27.112
Pretty much, if you get that wrong,

00:00:27.112 --> 00:00:28.822
you can get everything else perfect

00:00:28.822 --> 00:00:29.923
and we see this all the time.

00:00:29.923 --> 00:00:32.577
We see startups that hire the
best lawyer in the valley.

00:00:32.577 --> 00:00:34.181
They get a beautiful office.

00:00:34.181 --> 00:00:38.329
They work with really great
accountants and a great PR firm.

00:00:38.329 --> 00:00:41.213
They do everything that
a startup needs to do,

00:00:41.213 --> 00:00:46.105
except build a product that
customers or users want

00:00:46.105 --> 00:00:47.929
and this is so important.

00:00:47.929 --> 00:00:49.891
This is probably the most important piece

00:00:49.891 --> 00:00:52.534
of startup advice in the early days.

00:00:52.534 --> 00:00:55.264
This is the only thing that
matters, you have to do this.

00:00:55.264 --> 00:00:57.279
You can ignore all the other advice.

00:00:57.279 --> 00:01:00.062
You can ignore all of the
crazy stuff that people do

00:01:00.062 --> 00:01:01.320
when they're trying to advise you

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:03.575
about how to set up a company.

00:01:03.575 --> 00:01:05.059
In fact, you should ignore most advice.

00:01:05.059 --> 00:01:07.312
Most startup advice is terrible.

00:01:07.312 --> 00:01:08.416
You should feel free to ignore

00:01:08.416 --> 00:01:10.536
any of this too, except this one thing.

00:01:10.536 --> 00:01:13.563
If your startup doesn't make
something the users want,

00:01:13.563 --> 00:01:16.207
the startup will never ever be successful.

00:01:16.207 --> 00:01:18.654
- Making something people
want is massively important

00:01:18.654 --> 00:01:21.340
and if you don't do it,
your company will fail,

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:23.325
but it's only half the equation.

00:01:23.325 --> 00:01:25.464
You also have to love what you're making.

00:01:25.464 --> 00:01:27.472
This is where you will
have ultimate success

00:01:27.472 --> 00:01:29.116
as an entrepreneur and it doesn't matter

00:01:29.116 --> 00:01:31.123
if you've gone to university
or business school

00:01:31.123 --> 00:01:33.384
or had a history with parents

00:01:33.384 --> 00:01:35.382
as entrepreneurs or any of that.

00:01:35.382 --> 00:01:38.367
Doesn't matter, this is the
single most important thing

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:40.435
to understand and it's easy.

00:01:40.435 --> 00:01:41.833
Anybody can pick it up.

00:01:41.833 --> 00:01:44.581
You will have success as an entrepreneur

00:01:44.581 --> 00:01:46.206
when you make something that people want,

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:50.304
you're providing value,
and you love what you do.

00:01:50.304 --> 00:01:52.023
These have to be intersected.

00:01:52.023 --> 00:01:53.259
They have to match.

00:01:53.259 --> 00:01:55.179
When you can combine
those two things together,

00:01:55.179 --> 00:01:56.976
you have a successful business

00:01:56.976 --> 00:01:59.838
'cause look what happens when
the two things don't align.

00:01:59.838 --> 00:02:02.474
If you're making something
that people want,

00:02:02.474 --> 00:02:05.840
but you don't love it, you're
never going to put in the work,

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.641
the effort, the grind to become the best

00:02:08.641 --> 00:02:10.196
because there's somebody who will also

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.577
make something people
want and does love it

00:02:12.577 --> 00:02:14.103
and they're always going to crush you.

00:02:14.103 --> 00:02:15.856
They're going to be
putting in 16 hour days

00:02:15.856 --> 00:02:18.369
and just dreaming about
it every single day

00:02:18.369 --> 00:02:19.514
and telling all their friends

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:21.112
and trying to find ways to make it work

00:02:21.112 --> 00:02:22.729
and for you, you don't
care enough about it

00:02:22.729 --> 00:02:25.100
'cause you don't love it, so
that model's not going to work.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.907
You may make a little bit of money

00:02:26.907 --> 00:02:28.219
'cause you see an opportunity,

00:02:28.219 --> 00:02:30.346
but it's never going to be the thing

00:02:30.346 --> 00:02:31.636
that will help you take off.

00:02:31.636 --> 00:02:33.059
It's never going to be
the best version of you

00:02:33.059 --> 00:02:34.059
because you're doing something

00:02:34.059 --> 00:02:35.537
that you're not passionate about.

00:02:35.537 --> 00:02:37.737
On the flip side, if you're
doing something that you love

00:02:37.737 --> 00:02:41.358
but is useless to other people,
then you've got a hobby.

00:02:41.358 --> 00:02:43.180
That's great, go out and do
that thing that you love,

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:45.826
but if you can't find a way to add value

00:02:45.826 --> 00:02:47.341
to other people's lives and make something

00:02:47.341 --> 00:02:49.073
that they would actually pay for,

00:02:49.073 --> 00:02:50.324
you don't have a business either

00:02:50.324 --> 00:02:51.780
and so the ultimate success comes

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:54.522
when you can combine
those two things together.

00:02:54.522 --> 00:02:56.499
You got the thing that adds
value to people's lives

00:02:56.499 --> 00:03:00.259
and that people really
want and you love doing it

00:03:00.259 --> 00:03:03.506
and as long as those two
things are in harmony,

00:03:03.506 --> 00:03:05.823
then you've got a massively
successful business

00:03:05.823 --> 00:03:08.631
that could change the course of your life

00:03:08.631 --> 00:03:10.295
and the people around you as well.

00:03:10.295 --> 00:03:12.420
So, the question of the
day today is I'm curious

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:14.886
are you making something
that people actually want?

00:03:14.886 --> 00:03:16.058
Are you there yet?

00:03:16.058 --> 00:03:18.105
Are you getting great feedback yet?

00:03:18.105 --> 00:03:19.883
I'm curious, leave it
in the comments below

00:03:19.883 --> 00:03:21.028
and I'll join in the discussion.

00:03:21.028 --> 00:03:23.398
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Herman Pienaar.

00:03:23.398 --> 00:03:24.893
Herman, thank you so much for picking up

00:03:24.893 --> 00:03:26.809
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:03:26.809 --> 00:03:28.618
It really really really means a lot to me

00:03:28.618 --> 00:03:30.243
and I hope you're enjoying the read.

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.919
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:03:31.919 --> 00:03:33.010
I believe in you.

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:34.932
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:03:34.932 --> 00:03:37.109
and whatever your one word is

00:03:37.109 --> 00:03:38.491
and I'll see you again tomorrow morning

